id: shifted-poisonous
name: Shifted (Poisonous)
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock: the Square keeps the Quality until the last Environment Shift's clock runs out.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry gives the Squares a Quality and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held (environments.mjs qualitiesFromEffects).
quality: poisonous
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Environment Shift made your Square Poisonous until the start of its user's next turn.
text: >
  Shifted (Poisonous): Environment Shift's mark. "Those Squares gain one of the following Environmental Qualities until the
  start of your next turn: Aflame, Bouncy, Dangerous, Electrified, Frozen, or Poisonous."

---

# A mark rather than a tick in the Battlefields tab's list, as Ignited is: it runs out on the user's clock, and the list
# stays the player's. What the ground does is the Poisonous Quality's own file.
